WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.979 --> 00:00:05.100
If you're a gamer, you probably still have
some of your games for various Nintendo consoles

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:10.419
stashed away in your closet, along with your
Lisa Frank Trapper Keeper or your old Transformers.

00:00:10.419 --> 00:00:14.249
Parting with these classics could earn some
cold hard cash—for the right titles, of

00:00:14.249 --> 00:00:15.249
course.

00:00:15.249 --> 00:00:18.740
These price estimates are based on video game
price charting sites and recent eBay auctions,

00:00:18.740 --> 00:00:20.909
and focus only on games that have been used.

00:00:20.909 --> 00:00:25.210
If you kept your games sealed in their original
boxes, you were probably a really boring kid...but

00:00:25.210 --> 00:00:27.410
obviously sealed games are worth a whole lot
more.

00:00:27.410 --> 00:00:30.099
So, what’s worth the most today?

00:00:30.099 --> 00:00:32.020
Bonk's Adventure

00:00:32.020 --> 00:00:36.210
Originally released for the doomed TurboGrafx-16
console, Bonk's Adventure’s developers ported

00:00:36.210 --> 00:00:39.970
this quirky 2D platformer to the NES in 1994.

00:00:39.970 --> 00:00:43.809
In the game, you control Bonk, a hard-headed
caveboy who battles prehistoric enemies by

00:00:43.809 --> 00:00:46.309
literally head-butting them to death.

00:00:46.309 --> 00:00:49.910
If you've got a copy of Bonk's Adventure for
the NES hiding in your collection, it's worth

00:00:49.910 --> 00:00:53.280
quite a few bones—about $400 for the cartridge.

00:00:53.280 --> 00:00:54.790
Bubble Bobble Part 2

00:00:54.790 --> 00:00:58.250
The second installment in the Bubble Bobble
series sees the return of Bub and Bob, a pair

00:00:58.250 --> 00:01:01.670
of humans-turned-dragons who must make their
way through increasingly difficult stages

00:01:01.670 --> 00:01:04.059
by barfing out bubbles to trap their enemies.

00:01:04.059 --> 00:01:07.880
The gameplay is similar to other Bubble Bobble
games, although the NES version also includes

00:01:07.880 --> 00:01:12.610
bonus stages, in case you ever wanted to play
bubble dragon volleyball, which probably isn’t

00:01:12.610 --> 00:01:13.610
a euphemism.

00:01:13.610 --> 00:01:17.590
A Bubble Bobble Part 2 cartridge is worth
approximately $300.

00:01:17.590 --> 00:01:18.590
Panic Restaurant

00:01:18.590 --> 00:01:23.070
It’s a literal food fight when Chef Cookie
has to battle his way through six levels filled

00:01:23.070 --> 00:01:26.630
with food-beasts, with nothing but a frying
pan and a stylish mustache.

00:01:26.630 --> 00:01:30.370
The game features some of the most seriously
deranged box art of all time, but even if

00:01:30.370 --> 00:01:35.580
you've only got a loose copy of Panic Restaurant,
it's worth around $540...or one night with

00:01:35.580 --> 00:01:36.770
Gordon Ramsay.

00:01:36.770 --> 00:01:38.420
Aero Fighters

00:01:38.420 --> 00:01:41.530
Games where you pilot fighter planes are a
dime a dozen, but Aero Fighters stands out

00:01:41.530 --> 00:01:44.650
by being one of the rarest titles ever released
for Super NES.

00:01:44.650 --> 00:01:48.320
Though its gameplay is predictable and critics
of the day called this version mediocre, the

00:01:48.320 --> 00:01:51.750
once-worthless cart became desirable simply
because there aren’t too many of them out

00:01:51.750 --> 00:01:52.750
there.

00:01:52.750 --> 00:01:56.490
This one comes in at $559 for the cartridge
alone...but you probably won’t want to waste

00:01:56.490 --> 00:01:58.370
too much time playing it.

00:01:58.370 --> 00:02:00.540
Hagane: The Final Conflict

00:02:00.540 --> 00:02:04.350
A side-scrolling action platformer for the
Super NIntendo featuring a cyborg ninja on

00:02:04.350 --> 00:02:05.660
a revenge quest?

00:02:05.660 --> 00:02:09.080
If you’re not already completely sold on
Hagane: The Final Conflict, it’s time to

00:02:09.080 --> 00:02:11.819
put your inner child on a milk carton, because
it’s missing.

00:02:11.819 --> 00:02:16.340
With a futuristic setting, challenging stages,
and advanced controls, Hagane has become a

00:02:16.340 --> 00:02:17.340
cult classic.

00:02:17.340 --> 00:02:21.430
Currently, you could get around $475 for a
loose cartridge.

00:02:21.430 --> 00:02:22.819
Metal Warriors

00:02:22.819 --> 00:02:27.409
Stomp down puny humans, smash through walls,
and blast giant robots while piloting a mech

00:02:27.409 --> 00:02:30.160
assault suit in the Super Nintendo game Metal
Warriors.

00:02:30.160 --> 00:02:33.849
It's set in a dystopian future where the remaining
"Metal Warriors" defend the earth from the

00:02:33.849 --> 00:02:35.769
evil Dark Axis forces.

00:02:35.769 --> 00:02:40.569
If you've got a copy, it can fetch you about
$200, or about one one-millionth of the cost

00:02:40.569 --> 00:02:43.200
to buy a robot death machine of your very
own.

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:44.999
Worms: Armageddon

00:02:44.999 --> 00:02:48.609
You control a team of angry worms in this
turn-based military strategy game for the

00:02:48.609 --> 00:02:50.079
Nintendo 64.

00:02:50.079 --> 00:02:53.890
As you advance through your annelid enemies,
you can upgrade and gain new weapons, including

00:02:53.890 --> 00:02:57.060
the "Holy Hand Grenade" from the film Monty
Python and the Holy Grail.

00:02:57.060 --> 00:03:02.749
Currently, the game is worth approximately
$200, or twenty-five pounds of nightcrawlers.

00:03:02.749 --> 00:03:05.459
Bomberman 64: The Second Attack

00:03:05.459 --> 00:03:09.549
In this sequel to Bomberman 64, you control
Bomberman on an action adventure to save the

00:03:09.549 --> 00:03:12.680
world from possessed knights, demons, and
even a goddess.

00:03:12.680 --> 00:03:16.810
While the game does not have graphics on par
with some of the other N64 titles of its era,

00:03:16.810 --> 00:03:21.180
Bomberman 64: The Second Attack does give
Bomberman a backstory...if you really want

00:03:21.180 --> 00:03:24.310
a complex history of a guy who’s mostly
fun because he blows stuff up.

00:03:24.310 --> 00:03:26.250
You can sell this game for about $150.

00:03:26.250 --> 00:03:29.060
Cubivore: Survival of the Fittest

00:03:29.060 --> 00:03:33.049
Cubivore is an action-adventure title where
you must guide your floppy, cubic avatar through

00:03:33.049 --> 00:03:37.249
the world and make it stronger by devouring
other cubivores...or, strangely enough, mating

00:03:37.249 --> 00:03:39.999
with them in the game’s convenient “love
tunnel.”

00:03:39.999 --> 00:03:43.551
You absorb their power or make more powerful
babies, and you remorselessly consume and

00:03:43.551 --> 00:03:47.920
impregnate your fellow creatures until you
can take on the big boss, Killer Cubivore.

00:03:47.920 --> 00:03:52.810
Cubivore can net you about $130 for the Gamecube
disc alone, or about the price of a visit

00:03:52.810 --> 00:03:54.590
to a real love tunnel.

00:03:54.590 --> 00:03:55.889
Shantae

00:03:55.889 --> 00:04:00.279
The first in the Shantae series of platformers,
you guide Shantae, a half-genie, on her fight

00:04:00.279 --> 00:04:04.269
against a dastardly female pirate with a terrible
name, Risky Boots.

00:04:04.269 --> 00:04:08.590
The series has been wildly popular since its
first release in 2002, with a fourth installment

00:04:08.590 --> 00:04:11.170
in the series set to be released in late 2016.

00:04:11.170 --> 00:04:14.749
If you're lucky enough to have wished for
a copy for the Gameboy Color handheld console,

00:04:14.749 --> 00:04:18.250
you could sell the cartridge today for $290.

00:04:18.250 --> 00:04:19.250
Thanks for watching!

00:04:19.250 --> 00:04:22.030
Subscribe to our YouTube channel to watch
more videos like the one you just saw.

00:04:22.030 --> 00:04:24.910
And leave us a comment to let us know which
valuable games you’ve found in your closet….

